Q: Is there a better way to count occurrence of char in a string? A: <p>Here is another way which also works for muliple characters:</p>
<pre><code>my $str = 'abracadabra';
my $target = 'ab';
my $count = scalar(split(/\Q$target\E/, $str)) - 1;
</code></pre>

Q: C implicit const casting (in dereferencing order) should be permitted but isn&#39;t A: <p>Some example code to illustrate the issue.</p>
<pre class="lang-c prettyprint-override"><code>void foo(const char *const*p) {
  (void) p;
}

void bar(void) {
  char **p1;
  foo(p1); //  error: passing argument 1 of 'foo' from incompatible pointer type [-Wincompatible-pointer-types]
           //  note: expected 'const char * const*' but argument is of type 'char **'
  char *const*p2;
  foo(p2); // error: passing argument 1 of 'foo' from incompatible pointer type [-Wincompatible-pointer-types]
           // note: expected 'const char * const*' but argument is of type 'char * const*'
  const char **p3;
  foo(p3); // OK
  const char *const*p4;
  foo(p4); // OK
}
</code></pre>
